<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Benchmarks.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MetaWorld MT50</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">McLean et al. (2025)</a></cite> provides <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> manipulation tasks grouped into four difficulty tiers (Easy, Medium, Hard, Very Hard; Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Task Difficulty Partition for MetaWorld MT50 ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>); we use it as the primary long-horizon testbed, with planning horizons up to <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H{=}30</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LIBERO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2023)</a></cite> provides four task suites (Spatial, Object, Goal, Long), with the Long suite targeting extended-horizon manipulation. <span id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Real-world Piper.</span> A 6-DoF arm with a parallel gripper performs three tasks: <em id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pick Banana</em> (rigid grasping), <em id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Fold Cloth</em> (long-horizon deformable manipulation), and <em id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pull Drawer</em> (articulated object). Each task is evaluated with <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> trials under clean conditions, with an additional perceptual-robustness check under lighting shifts, positional perturbations, and <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> unseen distractors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We instantiate OneWM-VLA on top of <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Black et al. (2026)</a></cite>, with PaliGemma-2B as the vision-language backbone and Gemma-300M as the joint latent-and-action expert. Both are trained with LoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2022)</a></cite>. Flow matching uses <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> ODE steps at inference, with loss weights <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{a}{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{a}{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{r}{=}\lambda_{w_{1}}{=}\lambda_{w_{2}}{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{r}{=}\lambda_{w_{1}}{=}\lambda_{w_{2}}{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. We train for <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math>K steps on <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> NVIDIA A800 GPUs. On MetaWorld we evaluate <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\{5,10,25,30\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\{5,10,25,30\}</annotation></semantics></math>. On LIBERO we use a single training checkpoint (training action horizon <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>) for all four suites and tune only the inference action horizon and the replan step per suite on a small validation grid (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Inference-Time Configuration on LIBERO ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>). <span id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span>
We compare against <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (2B) and the larger <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> (3B) as the primary VLA references, and additionally report standard reference points (Diffusion Policy, ACT, Octo, OpenVLA, SpatialVLA, CoT-VLA, WorldVLA, <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-FAST, SmolVLA, GR00T-N1, DreamVLA) where available.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Main Results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MetaWorld MT50.</span> Tab. <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> reports four planning horizons. OneWM-VLA improves over <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> at every horizon, and the gap widens with <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. At <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H{=}30</annotation></semantics></math>, OneWM-VLA reaches <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="53.13\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>53.13</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">53.13\%</annotation></semantics></math> on average, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> drops to <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="37.98\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>37.98</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">37.98\%</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="26.83\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>26.83</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26.83\%</annotation></semantics></math>. The improvement is concentrated on the Hard and Very Hard tiers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LIBERO.</span> Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports the four suites. OneWM-VLA reaches <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="98.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>98.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">98.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> on average, above <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="96.85\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>96.85</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">96.85\%</annotation></semantics></math>). On the Long suite, OneWM-VLA reaches <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.6\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+10.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+10.4</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+3.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+3.2</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>. All four suites use the same training checkpoint; only the inference action horizon and the replan step are tuned per suite (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Inference-Time Configuration on LIBERO ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Real-world Piper.</span> Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports results on the physical robot. Among the three tasks, <em id="S5.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Fold Cloth</em> is the most demanding: the cloth state evolves continuously under contact, and the policy must remain stable across a long sequence of fine-grained interactions. Under clean conditions, OneWM-VLA reaches <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="71.7\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>71.7</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">71.7\%</annotation></semantics></math> on average, <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+21.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>21.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+21.7</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+13.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>13.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+13.4</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the largest absolute gain on <em id="S5.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Fold Cloth</em> (<math id="S5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.0\%</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20.0\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>25.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25.0\